  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and rationale\n\nWe use an analytical gradient-based optimization approach to minimize the maximum overlap integral \\( C_5 \\). The method employs the scipy.optimize.minimize function with the SLSQP algorithm, leveraging analytical gradients and efficiently handling constraints. This strategy provides a structured and efficient way to explore the solution space and find an improved upper bound.\n\n### 2. Mathematical specification\n\n- **Objective Function**: \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\left( \\sum_{i} h[i](1 - h[i+k]) \\right) \\times dx \\)\n- **Gradient**: For each \\( h[j] \\), \\( \\frac{\\partial C_5}{\\partial h[j]} = dx \\times \\left( (1 - h[j + k_{\\text{max}}]) - h[j - k_{\\text{max}}] \\right) \\) where \\( k_{\\text{max}} \\) is the shift that maximizes the overlap.\n- **Constraints**:\n  1. \\( 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\) for all \\( i \\)\n  2. \\( \\sum h = \\frac{n_{points}}{2} \\)\n\n### 3. Implementation procedure\n\n1. **Initialization**:\n   - Read initial guess if available, interpolate to \\( n_{points} = 100 \\), clip to [0,1], and scale to meet the sum constraint.\n\n2. **Objective and Gradient**:\n   - Compute \\( C_5 \\) using convolution.\n   - Compute analytical gradient for the current maximum overlap shift.\n\n3. **Optimization Setup**:\n   - Use scipy.optimize.minimize with SLSQP, providing bounds and sum constraint.\n\n4. **Execution**:\n   - Run optimization, track best solution, and handle constraints.\n\n### 4. Search choices and useful variations\n\n- **Initial Guess**: Use available initial values or uniform distribution.\n- **Solver**: SLSQP for constrained optimization.\n- **Parameters**: Max iterations set to 1000, tolerance to \\( 1e-8 \\).\n\n### 5. Compute budget and robustness\n\n- The optimization is expected to run within 600 seconds due to efficient gradient computation and SLSQP's effectiveness with constraints.\n\n### 6. Validation and return contract\n\n- Ensure \\( h \\) satisfies constraints and re-evaluate \\( C_5 \\) to confirm optimality.",
